WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.820
We learn words like wise and father
from finite things we can see and share.

2
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.810
Yet classical theists
believe God is infinite,

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.760
timeless, and not a physical object.

4
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:15.930
Can a word learned in time
describe a God outside time?

5
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:20.340
So can you describe God by
saying only what God is not?

6
00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:24.940
In this mission, you'll meet two ways
a word like wise might apply to God,

7
00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.200
and the danger lurking in each.

8
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.540
Then you'll read what Thomas
Aquinas made of those two dangers,

9
00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.810
in his great work on God.

10
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:38.110
Your mission: find out whether speaking
of God only by denial can really work.
